ine with \\n for newlines. Also double quotes inside the source are escaped as \\\". Also backslashes need to be escaped, but in the source we don't have any backslashes except in the lambda? No. So it's fine.\n\nWe need to ensure that the JSON is valid. We'll produce the final response as a JSON object.\n\nLet's write the implementation string carefully.\n\ndef solve(case):\n    payload = case[\"payload\"]\n    nodes = payload[\"nodes\"]\n    required_symbols = set(payload[\"required_symbols\"])\n    node_map = {node[\"id\"]: node for node in nodes}\n    children = {node[\"id\"]: [] for node in nodes}\n    for node in nodes:\n        pid = node.get(\"parent\")\n        if pid is not None:\n            children[pid].append(node[\"id\"])\n    retained = set(node[\"id\"] for node in nodes)\n    sorted_nodes = sorted(nodes, key=lambda n: (-n[\"depth\"], n[\"id\"]))\n    removal_order = []\n    for node in sorted_nodes:\n        nid = node[\"id\"]\n        if node[\"parent\"] is None:\n            continue\n        if not node[\"removable\"]:\n            continue\n        if node[\"symbol\"] in required_symbols:\n            continue\n        has_retained_children = any(cid in retained for cid in children[nid])\n        if has_retained_children:\n            continue\n        remaining_symbols = set()\n        for rid in retained:\n            if rid != nid:\n                remaining_symbols.add(node_map[rid][\"symbol\"])\n        if not required_symbols.issubset(remaining_symbols):\n            continue\n        retained.remove(nid)\n        removal_order.append(nid)\n    sorted_retained = sorted(retained)\n    return {\"retained\": sorted_retained, \"removal_order\": removal_order}\n\nNow escape for JSON: replace all double quotes with \\\", replace newlines with \\n. Also ensure no trailing spaces. I'll produce the JSON string.\n\nI'll write the JSON object as:\n\n{\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    payload = case[\\\"payload\\\"]\\n    nodes = payload[\\