r node in nodes}\\n    children = {node[\"id\"]: [] for node in nodes}\\n    for node in nodes:\\n        pid = node.get(\"parent\")\\n        if pid is not None:\\n            children[pid].append(node[\"id\"])\\n    retained = set(node[\"id\"] for node in nodes)\\n    sorted_nodes = sorted(nodes, key=lambda n: (-n[\"depth\"], n[\"id\"]))\\n    removal_order = []\\n    for node in sorted_nodes:\\n        nid = node[\"id\"]\\n        if node[\"parent\"] is None:\\n            continue\\n        if not node[\"removable\"]:\\n            continue\\n        if node[\"symbol\"] in required_symbols:\\n            continue\\n        has_retained_children = any(cid in retained for cid in children[nid])\\n        if has_retained_children:\\n            continue\\n        remaining_symbols = set()\\n        for rid in retained:\\n            if rid != nid:\\n                remaining_symbols.add(node_map[rid][\"symbol\"])\\n        if not required_symbols.issubset(remaining_symbols):\\n            continue\\n        retained.remove(nid)\\n        removal_order.append(nid)\\n    sorted_retained = sorted(retained)\\n    return {\"retained\": sorted_retained, \"removal_order\": removal_order}'\n\nThen we need to JSON-escape it. Since we are writing the response directly, we need to manually replace \" with \\\", and also newlines with \\n. That gives a long string. But we can also use Python to generate the JSON, but we are the assistant, we just output text. So I'll produce the escaped version.\n\nI'll write the JSON object in a code block? No, the response must be exactly the JSON object with no markdown. So I'll just output the JSON string.\n\nLet me construct it carefully.\n\nI'll write:\n\n{\"implementation\":\"def solve(case):\\n    payload = case[\\\"payload\\\"]\\n    nodes = payload[\\\"nodes\\\"]\\n    required_symbols = set(payload[\\\"required_symbols\\\"])\\n    node_map = {node[\\\"id\\\"]: node for node in nodes}\\n    children = {node[\\\"id\\\"]: [] for node in nodes}\\n    for node in nodes:\\n        pid = node.get(\\\"parent\\\")\\n        if pid is not None:\\n            children[pid].append(node[\\\"id\\\"])\\n    retained = set(node[\\\"id\\\"] for node in nodes)\\n    sorted_nodes = sorted(nodes, key=lambda n: (-n[\\\"depth\\\"], n[\\\"id\\\"]))\\n    removal_order = []\\n    for node in sorted_nodes:\\n        nid = node[\\\"id\\\"]\\n        if node[\\\"parent\\\"] is None:\\n            continue\\n        if not node[\\\"removable\\\"]:\\n            continue\\n        if node[\\\"symbol\\\"] in required_symbols:\\n            continue\\n        has_retained_children = any(cid in retained for cid in children[nid])\\n        if has_retained_children:\\n            continue\\n        remaining_symbols = set()\\n        for rid in retained:\\n            if rid != nid:\\n                remaining_symbols.add(node_map[rid][\\\"symbol\\\"])\\n        if not required_symbols.issubset(remaining_symbols):\\n            continue\\n        retained.remove(nid)\\n        removal_order.append(nid)\\n    sorted_retained = sorted(retained)\\n    return {\\\"retained\\\": sorted_retained, \\\"removal_order\\\": removal_order}\"}\n\nI need to ensure that all double quotes inside the string are escaped. In the above, I used \\\". But note: in the source, we have e.g., case[\"payload\"] becomes case[\\\"payload\\\"] in JSON. That seems correct. Also the lambda uses double quotes around \"depth\" and \"id\". They are escaped. The last return uses double quotes around \"retained\" and \"removal_order\". Those are also escaped.\n\nCheck for any unescaped double quotes: The string starts with \" and ends with \". Inside, every double quote is preceded by a backslash. So it's valid.\n\nAlso newlines are represented as \\n. So the entire string is on one line in JSON, but when parsed, it will have newlines.\n\nThus the JSON object is ready.\n\nBut we must ensure the first non-whitespace character is { and last is }. The above starts with { and ends with \"}. So that's fine.\n\nI'll output that."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":1849,"completion_tokens":6134,"total_tokens":7983,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":1792},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":5747},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":1792,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":57},"system_fingerprint":"fp_8b330d02d0_prod0820_fp8_kvcache_20260402"}